  "description": "NASA’s annual Day of Remembrance pays tribute to all members of the NASA family who lost their lives in the pursuit of exploration and discovery, including test pilots, the crews of Apollo 1 and space shuttles Challenger and Columbia. On Jan. 23, 2025, we pause to honor their memory and reflect on the importance of maintaining a strong safety culture.",
